# clangd fallback config. The robust source of truth is compile_commands.json
# (run `make compile-commands`); this file makes clangd correct even before that
# is generated, and mirrors the build's gate so warnings surface as must-fix
# errors.
#
# Why each flag:
#   -I<repo root>  absolute on purpose — clangd resolves a relative `-I.` against
#                  its own cwd (often the edited file's dir), not the repo root,
#                  so `-I.` left `#include "core/run.h"` unresolved and cascaded
#                  fake "undeclared identifier" errors (u64/Sig/RunRecord/SIGMAX).
#   -std=c++20 -xc++   match the build; -xc++ forces C++ for the .h headers.
#   -Wall -Wextra -Werror   mirror the Makefile gate: a real warning shows as an
#                  editor error, never an ignorable squiggle.
#   -DGIT_REV/-DBUILD_TIME   make injects these per build; define them (value is
#                  irrelevant to analysis) so they don't read as undeclared.
CompileFlags:
  Add:
    - -I/Users/jasonp/src/polyominoes
    - -std=c++20
    - -xc++
    - -Wall
    - -Wextra
    - -Werror
    - -DGIT_REV="dev"
    - -DBUILD_TIME="dev"
